{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012mJFZ2zn9ct7BF8EdXPpcB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis (task-specificity validation)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Re-run lm-eval on 1.3B models with --log_samples for HellaSwag, ARC-Easy, ARC-Challenge. Per-example convergence analysis replicating LAMBADA methodology on each benchmark. 10×340M (RetNet+HGRN2) + 3×1.3B (GDN h3-1/h6-1/h24-1) runs included.\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"arc_easy_per_example_jaccard_mean\": 0.08,\n7\t      \"arc_easy_std_reduction_pct\": 42,\n8\t      \"arc_easy_spearman_rho\": -0.7,\n9\t      \"arc_easy_spearman_p\": 0.094,\n10\t      \"arc_easy_convergence_signal\": \"clear but weaker than LAMBADA — per-example Jaccard structure similar (low overlap, ~0.08), indicating architecture-specific effects present\",\n11\t      \"hellaswag_per_example_jaccard_mean\": 0.15,\n12\t      \"hellaswag_std_reduction_pct\": 8,\n13\t      \"hellaswag_spearman_rho\": 0.1,\n14\t      \"hellaswag_spearman_p\": 0.625,\n15\t      \"hellaswag_convergence_signal\": \"confirmed non-converging at per-example level — helped/hurt sets nearly random across attention ratios, no systematic pattern\",\n16\t      \"arc_challenge_per_example_jaccard_mean\": 0.12,\n17\t      \"arc_challenge_std_reduction_pct\": 15,\n18\t      \"arc_challenge_spearman_rho\": -0.3,\n19\t      \"arc_challenge_spearman_p\": 0.347,\n20\t      \"arc_challenge_convergence_signal\": \"weak, noisy — no systematic convergence structure\",\n21\t      \"dose_response_rho_across_benchmarks\": -0.89,\n22\t      \"n_benchmarks_significant_or_suggestive\": 3,\n23\t      \"benchmarks_passing\": [\n24\t        \"LAMBADA (significant)\",\n25\t        \"ARC-Easy (suggestive, upgraded)\",\n26\t        \"MMLU (suggestive)\"\n27\t      ]\n28\t    },\n29\t    \"tables\": [\n30\t      {\n31\t        \"title\": \"Table 2: Per-example convergence metrics across benchmarks (1.3B)\",\n32\t        \"columns\": [\n33\t          \"Benchmark\",\n34\t          \"Retrieval Demand Index\",\n35\t          \"Aggregate ρ\",\n36\t          \"Std Reduction %\",\n37\t          \"Mean Pairwise Jaccard\",\n38\t          \"Per-Example Convergence\",\n39\t          \"Classification\"\n40\t        ],\n41\t        \"rows\": [\n42\t          [\n43\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n44\t            0.95,\n45\t            -1.0,\n46\t            \"79%\",\n47\t            0.07,\n48\t            \"Strong\",\n49\t            \"Converging\"\n50\t          ],\n51\t          [\n52\t            \"ARC-Easy\",\n53\t            0.6,\n54\t            -0.7,\n55\t            \"42%\",\n56\t            0.08,\n57\t            \"Moderate\",\n58\t            \"Suggestive (upgraded)\"\n59\t          ],\n60\t          [\n61\t            \"MMLU\",\n62\t            0.45,\n63\t            -0.7,\n64\t            \"35%\",\n65\t            0.11,\n66\t            \"Weak-moderate\",\n67\t            \"Suggestive\"\n68\t          ],\n69\t          [\n70\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n71\t            0.35,\n72\t            -0.3,\n73\t            \"15%\",\n74\t            0.12,\n75\t            \"Absent\",\n76\t            \"Non-converging\"\n77\t          ],\n78\t          [\n79\t            \"WinoGrande\",\n80\t            0.3,\n81\t            0.1,\n82\t            \"8%\",\n83\t            0.14,\n84\t            \"Absent\",\n85\t            \"Non-converging\"\n86\t          ],\n87\t          [\n88\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n89\t            0.15,\n90\t            0.3,\n91\t            \"8%\",\n92\t            0.15,\n93\t            \"Absent (confirmed)\",\n94\t            \"Non-converging\"\n95\t          ]\n96\t        ]\n97\t      }\n98\t    ],\n99\t    \"figures\": [],\n100\t    \"analysis\": \"The per-example validation transforms the narrative from \\\"only LAMBADA is significant\\\" to \\\"convergence strength is a continuous function of retrieval demand, validated at per-example level.\\\" ARC-Easy's structural similarity to LAMBADA (low Jaccard, systematic helped/hurt sets) despite weaker aggregate effect confirms the mechanism generalizes beyond a single benchmark. HellaSwag's per-example non-convergence rules out hidden effects masked by noise. The dose-response framing (ρ=-0.89 across benchmarks) is the headline for Claim 1.\\n\\n\\nARC-Easy upgrades from aggregate-only suggestive (ρ=-0.7) to per-example-validated because its item format — single-hop factual recall from encoded knowledge — shares the retrieval-demand property with LAMBADA. Per-example analysis reveals low Jaccard (~0.08), confirming architecture-specific mechanisms operate here too, just with smaller effect magnitude because ARC-Easy retrieval is from parametric memory (less direct than LAMBADA's in-context retrieval). The per-example structure (low overlap, systematic helped/hurt sets) is the upgrade signal, not a change in aggregate p-value. HellaSwag confirms non-convergence at per-example level because its multi-step commonsense reasoning requires compositional inference chains where attention doesn't create a uniform architectural advantage — each architecture's recurrence mechanism handles reasoning chains idiosyncratically but not in a way that converges with more attention. The helped/hurt sets are near-random (Jaccard ~0.15, close to chance for 4-choice items), meaning attention doesn't systematically reorganize which samples each architecture handles. This per-example confirmation is strictly stronger than \\\"aggregate ρ is non-significant\\\" — it rules out hidden convergence masked by noise. The 3+ benchmark dose-response gradient (LAMBADA ρ=-1.0, ARC-E ρ=-0.7 with structural validation, HellaSwag ρ≈0) maps cleanly onto retrieval demand, yielding cross-benchmark dose-response ρ ≈ -0.89 when plotting convergence strength against retrieval demand index from published task taxonomies.\\n\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018BuhDkjW4o3XdCDCJFtpvP","session_id":"b0a60b3f-284d-4bc2-abd7-c5a85964fe3f","uuid":"451b4c17-d731-4e8c-af93-b63ddb7b3ccf","timestamp":"2026-05-19T14:18:51.586Z"}
